{{/*
  APPROVED — ticket 12, variant B: a dot in the date gutter.

  Today keeps its date (every other row is identified by its date; the one row you are
  most likely to reference should not be the one that loses it). A solid gray-900 dot
  sits beside it. Nothing structural changes: the rails, the 28px rhythm, the five
  columns are all untouched.

  Deliberately gray-900, never blue — ticket 14 spends text-blue-500 on future dates,
  and today's row sits DIRECTLY BELOW the nearest future day. The two marks must not
  read as the same family.

  Chosen over:
    A — "Today" replacing the date. Costs today its date and breaks the gutter's
        tabular-nums alignment on that row.
    C — thickening the two rails for today's height. Darkens the lines ticket 08 spent
        real effort making uniform and unbroken; a heavier segment reads as a seam.

  ---- WHY THIS ROW IS MARKED AT ALL ----

  Ticket 14 REQUIRES it. There is no Upcoming section — the ledger runs continuously
  from the future into the past — so today's row is the ONLY boundary between "hasn't
  happened yet" and "already spent".

  ---- TODAY WHEN EMPTY (the common case) ----

  Today's empty row does NOT recede. Ticket 01's muted italic grey exists to push days
  that are DONE WITH into the background; today is not done with. It is the row the
  user opened the app to fill.

  Same 28px row, same structure, same whole-row add target — only the ink weight
  changes:

                     other empty day          today, empty
    copy             "no expenses"            "no expenses yet"
    copy class       text-gray-300 italic     text-gray-500
    the +            text-gray-400            text-gray-900

  ---- WHAT CARRIES IT ----

  The mark is a property of the DAY, not of the page: it means "this day is today", not
  "this is the timeline's boundary". Drawing the boundary is what it happens to DO on
  the timeline; it is not what it IS.

  So the shared day partial compares page data itself — nothing is threaded, and the
  two consumers cannot drift:

      {{if eq .Date $.Today}}   → the dot

  basePageData already puts Today in PageData on EVERY page (handlers_html.go:71), so
  both the timeline and ticket 05's ?date= filter view get it for free. The dot appears
  wherever the day appears, ?date=<today> included.

  There is still NO IsToday field on domain.DailyGroup — ticket 04 refused one and that
  refusal stands. Ticket 04 predicted this exact mechanism when it deferred the
  question; the prediction held.

  In the markup below, `.isToday` is shorthand for that comparison — it is NOT a
  parameter the caller supplies.

  See .plan/daily-timeline/tickets/12-todays-row.md
*/}}

{{/* ---- The date gutter, for a populated day ---- */}}
<div class="w-28 shrink-0 pt-2 pb-2">
  {{if .isToday}}
  <div class="py-1.5 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs tabular-nums font-semibold text-gray-900 whitespace-nowrap leading-4">
    <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-gray-900 shrink-0"></span>
    {{shortDate .date .tz}}
  </div>
  {{else}}
  <div class="py-1.5 text-xs tabular-nums {{if .future}}text-blue-500{{else if .populated}}font-semibold text-gray-900{{else}}text-gray-400{{end}} whitespace-nowrap leading-4">
    {{shortDate .date .tz}}
  </div>
  {{end}}
</div>

{{/* ---- The expenses column of an EMPTY day. Today's does not recede. ---- */}}
<div class="flex-1 min-w-0 self-start pt-2 pb-2 pl-2 pr-2">
  <a
    href="/expenses/new?date={{.date}}"
    aria-label="Add expense on {{.label}}"
    class="group flex items-center px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md hover:bg-blue-50 transition-colors"
  >
    <span class="text-xs {{if .isToday}}text-gray-500{{else}}text-gray-300 italic{{end}} leading-4 group-hover:text-blue-600"
      >no expenses{{if .isToday}} yet{{end}}</span
    >
    <span class="flex-1"></span>
    <span class="text-lg leading-4 {{if .isToday}}text-gray-900{{else}}text-gray-400{{end}} group-hover:text-blue-600">+</span>
  </a>
</div>
